    "full": {
      "resp": "# Instruction-bound.\n\n`qtip2b_grouped_gemm` is **ISSUE-BOUND** \u2014 75% issue-active, only 5% DRAM, 38% occupancy \u2014 and the verdict on record is that no kernel fix reaches it; only a cheaper-to-decode format does.\n\nFor b=1 specifically, the same conclusion was reached separately for the FP8 GEMV: `fp8_gemv_warp` is **instruction-bound**, not memory-latency-bound, because of a per-4-byte integer divide (`k / block_size_x`, signed, non-const parameter). The ceiling works out to 1.5\u20133.0 TB/s against a ~4.0 TB/s achievable memory roof \u2014 under the roof at both ends, so instruction-bound *a fortiori*.\n\nNote the correction that came with it: the earlier \"4% memory-controller utilisation \u21d2 latency-bound\" story is **retracted**. And the b=1 step also carries a 30.5% host-sampler share plus an unprofiled 9.5% softmax_f32 \u2014 host overhead, not memory latency.",
